Building the Cathedral requires the {{technology|Reinforced Concrete}} tech. The in-game requirement says something about rebuilding it three times, but if you just complete this construction and wait a bit it seems to trigger.
{{icon|ibtwb|w=36px}}

- id=\"Portugal Is Not a Small Country!\"

You can add on Threaten Hostilities to a treaty that would've already been accepted to get it easily.
{{icon|tgwb|w=36px}}

- id=\"Kobu Gattai\"

Easy to do at game start as Morocco, thanks to their starting navy. The AI doesn't seem to close the Danish straits and Russia and Sweden don't really seem to defend themselves, so it should be quick to obtain.
{{icon|tgwb|w=36px}}

- id=\"Mikasa es su Casa\"

Noda Shoyu Co, Kinkozan Sobei and Mitsui are the best companies if aiming just to get this achievement fast, as they have profitable industries for the early game and prestige goods that are produced the moment they become prosperous.
{{icon|coc|w=36px}}

- id=\"Three Mountains\"

After achieving independence, with some relations improvement {{flag|Russia}} will usually be open to backing plays against Japan in exchange for Sakhalin. If done early enough, Japan will often fold without a fight. Japan may also get into a civil war, in which they may be willing to transfer their portion of Ryukyu if you're lucky.
{{icon|tgwb|w=36px}}

- id=\"Wealth, Fame, Power\"

Although it says privateering, piracy also counts & is much easier since it can be done at peace. Raiding the Malay Sea is very lucrative and you're unlikely to see many enemy ships. It's easiest to just start as Siam or Dain Nam, build a navy and have it do piracy until the achievement fires.
{{icon|tgwb|w=36px}}

